  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,1),(2,3),$ and $(5,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{\u2032}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(4,-1)$\n- $(17,-3)$\n- $(10,-1)$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{\u2032}$ are $(4,-1),(17,-3),(10,-1).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
